  "lineage": "Northern Chinese solo oral storytelling (pingshu, 'commentary-book'), in which a standing teller serialises long historical and martial-heroic novels — Romance of the Three Kingdoms, Water Margin, Generals of the Yang Family — over many nightly episodes, traditionally in teahouses using a folding fan, a handkerchief and a wooden waking-block (xingmu) rapped for emphasis. A Beijing-Tianjin Mandarin-language art distinct from the southern sung tanci, it reached mass audiences through radio and television, with Yuan Kuocheng and Shan Tianfang among its best-known twentieth-century masters. Delivery is vivid narrative speech with sudden gesture, mimicry and the crack of the block to mark suspense.",
